        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-15T16:15:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The CONFIG_F2FS_UNFAIR_RWSEM still goes to the down_read_trylock() case, so those hooks are exercised and can cause wait_event() to return control to f2fs_down_read().\n\nPlease explain why \"existing hooks cannot satisfy\". Could a hook be added in the \"normal\" path somewhere to avoid adding it in the inline function here?",
      "parentUuid": "bc539959_5e5c6702",
      "revId": "ca45cd69c96dd6905db98957f19f66f2c23cf70c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87dd8676_5fe96e79",
        "filename": "fs/f2fs/f2fs.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2183,
      "author": {
        "id": 3601150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T03:26:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It cannot be added in the \"normal\" path.\nreasons here:\n1, The rwsem source is difficult to be identified as the \"f2fs_rwsem\" in existing hooks of down_read_trylock; \n2, It doesn\u0027t always has a slowpath while down_read_trylock returns failed.\n\neg: down_read_trylock of f2fs_down_read_trylock just has a try, and priority policy is unnecessary here -- the key thread may not be blocked here; Once the rwsem owner\u0027s priority is changed, it is difficult to choose a chance to restore it later.\n\nThe priority policy is needed to change the f2fs rwsem owner\u0027s priority while key thread enters \u0027sleep\u0027 before, then restore the owner\u0027s priority until the key thread holds the lock successfully.\n\nThe new hook can cover the whole slowpath that the key thread hold f2fs lock.",
      "parentUuid": "f3eb9c1e_2ca1559a",
      "revId": "ca45cd69c96dd6905db98957f19f66f2c23cf70c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8babc51e_0b412791",
        "filename": "fs/f2fs/f2fs.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2183,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T17:24:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The rwsem source is difficult to be identified as the \"f2fs_rwsem\"\n\nWhy is that important? Isn\u0027t the point to avoid prio inversion? Why does it matter that this particular rwsem case is f2fs? Do you have different priority schemes for f2fs than other paths in the kernel? Why?\n\nI don\u0027t understand why f2fs needs special casing like this when there are hooks for the same purpose (prio inversion) in all of the locking primitives. Please give a detailed explanation why this kind of prio inversion is different than what can be handled with the many hooks that already exist in the rwsem primitives.",
      "parentUuid": "87dd8676_5fe96e79",
      "revId": "ca45cd69c96dd6905db98957f19f66f2c23cf70c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "292f8c63_cd017e49",
        "filename": "fs/f2fs/f2fs.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2183,
      "author": {
        "id": 3601150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T04:35:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is important for our prio policy, we want to limit the policy to work when key thread is blocked on f2fs rwsem.\n\nAs f2fs_down_read() chooses this way in our latest version:\n\u0027\u0027\u0027wait_event(sem-\u003eread_waiters, down_read_trylock(\u0026sem-\u003einternal_rwsem));\u0027\u0027\u0027\nand thread blocked here is decided by wait_event() and down_read_trylock(), so the new hook is designed to cover the whole slowpath, eg:f2fs_down_read will follow this way with new hook:\n‘‘\u0027\nif (down_read_trylock) return;\nimprove prio;\nwhile(1) {\n....   if (down_read_trylock) break;\n....  schedule;\n}\nrestore prio;\n’‘\u0027\nwe need to bypass wait_event in one new hook with the logic above, this is different with priority policy in normal rwsem;\neg: policy may need two hooks in rwsem_down_read_slowpath：\n’‘\u0027\nif (down_read_trylock) return;\nimprove prio; ------------ the first hook\nwhile(1) {\n....     if (smp_load_acquire) break;\n....     schedule;\n}\nrestore prio; ------------ the second hook\n’‘\u0027\nbut f2fs_down_read() doesn\u0027t enter rwsem_down_read_slowpath() for CONFIG_F2FS_UNFAIR_RWSEM is \u0027y\u0027;\n \nmore:\ndown_read_trylock() doesn\u0027t always need a priority policy, even it tries lock failed;\nthis is why the hooks in down_read_trylock() cannot be used in our policy.",
      "parentUuid": "8babc51e_0b412791",
      "revId": "ca45cd69c96dd6905db98957f19f66f2c23cf70c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
